Flux Lite is the free edition of Flux: the Windows standalone download, and the Microsoft Store edition used without the Pro add-on. Earlier versions call it "Free"; these terms apply to it under either name. Both forms of Flux Lite provide the features identified as Lite (or Free) in the supplied version, and both permit personal and internal business use without purchasing Pro. Payment unlocks Pro features; business use alone does not require Pro.

The Microsoft Store Pro add-on unlocks the Pro features identified in its offer. Microsoft Store manages its acquisition and ownership. Pro access requires a valid entitlement for the corresponding Store product. The standalone Flux Lite download does not accept Store Pro activation codes or import that entitlement. On Windows, the publisher does not currently offer Pro through any channel other than the Microsoft Store.

Flux Monitor Beta and a later production Store product can have different identities. A Beta entitlement does not promise a production entitlement unless the publisher expressly includes that right in the offer. No future price or paid upgrade follows from these terms alone.

The price and purchase conditions displayed before checkout govern a purchase, subject to applicable law. These terms do not authorize recurring charges. Refund, cancellation, and consumer rights remain subject to the purchase terms and applicable law. These terms do not add a refund promise of their own.

